{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/897573-quick-question-about-abjuration-and-the-claimed","id":897573,"title":"Quick Question about abjuration and the Claimed","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-23T22:06:32-07:00","id":897573,"title":"Quick Question about abjuration and the Claimed","content":"Finally getting ready to run my first game, so I'm actually reading through all the rules in detail for once. So hopefully someone here can help me out with a bit of confusion I'm having.<br /> <br /> Becoming Claimed is described as being utterly transformative and essentially permanent, to the point where even if the spirit breaks away (something requiring an opposed, and IIRC portrayed as fairly traumatic for it as well) it takes several days for the hosts appearance to become human again, and they retain the spirits virtue and vice. <br /> <br /> Abjuration, if it actually works, suppresses all conditions for a day. This presumably includes Claimed, but how does that actually happen? Is it as if the spirit successfully broke away? Is the human returned to a pre-Claimed state (human appearance, previous virtue and vice, no superhuman attributes)? When the abjuration expires, is the spirit instantly drawn back into the Claimed body, and do they have to begin reallocating ability points from scratch or does the Claimed get all their power back at once?<br /> <br /> Also, wouldn't it make more sense for the Claimed to resist abjuration with resolve+composure, the same way it does the spirit trying to break off on its own?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for any answers or advice people have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11821-st-just","name":"St.Just","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"19"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:22:52-07:00","id":905538,"title":"","content":"I'd say the spirit/ghost/goetic/angel that claimed someone is rendered dormant, not ejected from the host. So the hosts appear is the same, but the Claimed can't use their powers, and the personality is that of the mortal, but the spirit is still there, its just sleeping.<br /> <br /> When the abjuration runs out, the spirit/ghost/Goetic/Angels wake up and its business as usual, fused personality, influences,ect...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-02T04:25:51-07:00","id":905540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/897573-quick-question-about-abjuration-and-the-claimed?p=905538#post905538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say the spirit/ghost/goetic/angel that claimed someone is rendered dormant, not ejected from the host. So the hosts appear is the same, but the Claimed can't use their powers, and the personality is that of the mortal, but the spirit is still there, its just sleeping.<br /> <br /> When the abjuration runs out, the spirit/ghost/Goetic/Angels wake up and its business as usual, fused personality, influences,ect...</div> </div> </div> </div>Works, think of it like in The Rite movie where Hopkins' priest has to exorcize the kid over and over.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}